When generating a Git commit message for this repository, follow Conventional Commits in English.

Format: `<type>(<optional-scope>): <short summary>`

Types: feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, perf, test, build, ci, chore, revert

- Imperative mood; subject explains why, not a file list
- Subject ≤ 72 characters, lowercase after the colon, no trailing period
- Optional body: 1–2 sentences after a blank line; omit if the subject is enough
- Breaking change: type with `!` and/or a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer
- Do not mention AI or Cursor; no Co-authored-by unless asked

Good: `feat(search): rank custom keywords above default aliases`
Bad: `Updated files` / `Added Fuse.js and changed App.svelte`
